WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.200 align:middle line:90%

2
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:03.732 align:middle line:84%
I've got a milestone here that
I know needs to be finished.

3
00:00:03.732 --> 00:00:05.190 align:middle line:84%
And I have several
to-do lists that

4
00:00:05.190 --> 00:00:07.980 align:middle line:84%
need to be finished first
to complete this milestone.

5
00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:10.180 align:middle line:84%
Basecamp has a way to
relate those to each other

6
00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:12.720 align:middle line:84%
so I can see exactly
what needs to be done.

7
00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:15.540 align:middle line:84%
From the To-Do's tab, I'm
going to click on the red Edit

8
00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:17.470 align:middle line:90%
link for this list.

9
00:00:17.470 --> 00:00:20.700 align:middle line:84%
There's a section for relating
this list to a milestone here.

10
00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:23.340 align:middle line:84%
I'll select the right milestone
from the dropdown menu

11
00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:24.810 align:middle line:90%
and then click Save.

12
00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:28.350 align:middle line:84%
When I go back to the calendar,
I can click on this milestone

13
00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:30.390 align:middle line:90%
and now see that to-do list.

14
00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:31.980 align:middle line:84%
This lets me know
I need to finish

15
00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:35.600 align:middle line:84%
that list before I can mark
this milestone as complete.
